<h1>{cntx}

<p>{A markup format and parser between HTML and Markdown. Tags look like HTML. Content is wrapped in explicit curly-brace flow blocks instead of inferred block structure. Shorthand hash-id and dot-class syntax works alongside normal HTML-style attributes.}

<p>{The parser produces a typed AST. There is no renderer included in this package.}

<p>{Inspired by Pug, HTML, Markdown, and Pydoc-style string literals.}

<h2>{Usage}

<code lang="typescript">{{{
import { parse } from "cntx";

const document = parse(`<h1#heading>{Hello World}`);

console.log(document);
}}}

<p>{The parse function accepts a source string and returns a DocumentNode. It throws on invalid input.}

<h2>{Syntax overview}

<p>{A cntx document is a sequence of elements. Each element has:}

<ol>{
<li>{An opening tag with a name and optional attributes}
<li>{An optional block: flow content, a literal fence, or nothing}
}

<p>{There are no closing tags. Elements do not nest by indentation alone. To put content inside an element, open a flow block with an opening curly brace after the tag.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<h1>{Heading}

<p>{Hello World}

<img src="https://example.com/image.jpg">
}}}

<p>{Leading and trailing whitespace between top-level elements is ignored.}

<h3>{Comments}

<p>{Any tag whose name starts with ! is a comment. Comments use the same flow, literal fence, and empty blocks as elements, but they are not included in the AST.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<!>{this is a comment}

<!note>{{{
multiline comment
\}\}\}
}}}

<p>{To comment out markup without deleting it, prefix the tag name with !:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<!p class="muted">{hello <strong>{world}}
}}}

<p>{An explicit empty comment uses an empty flow block:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<!>{}
}}}

<p>{A bare comment tag with no block is also allowed and is treated as empty:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<!>
}}}

<p>{To comment out a following element, prefix that element tag name with ! instead of stacking a bare comment tag before it:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<!p>{hello}
}}}

<h3>{Tags}

<p>{Tags start with a less-than sign and end with the first unquoted greater-than sign. Tag names may contain letters, digits, and hyphens.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<h1>{Heading}
<p>{Paragraph}
<my-component>{Custom element}
}}}

<p>{An empty tag name is invalid:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<>
}}}

<h3>{Attributes}

<p>{Attributes appear inside the tag, after the tag name. Two styles can be combined on the same tag.}

<h4>{Shorthand id and class}

<p>{Pug-style shorthand is supported directly on the tag name:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<h1#heading-1>{Heading 1}
<p.large-text.lead>{Paragraph}
<div#app.container>{App shell}
}}}

<p>{Rules:}

<ul>{
<li>{Hash-id sets the id attribute}
<li>{Dot-class sets the class attribute}
<li>{Multiple dot-class segments are appended to the tag}
<li>{Hash and dot shorthand cannot appear without a tag name}
<li>{Empty hash or dot segments are invalid}
<li>{Only one id is allowed per tag}
}

<h4>{HTML-style attributes}

<p>{Standard space-separated attributes are supported:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<img src="photo.jpg" alt="A photo">
<button data-id="123" aria-label="Close" disabled>{Save}
<input type="text" required>
}}}

<p>{Rules:}

<ul>{
<li>{Valued attributes must use a quoted value with double quotes, single quotes, or backticks}
<li>{Unquoted values are not supported}
<li>{Boolean attributes are written as bare names and parse to empty strings}
<li>{Attribute names may include hyphens, digits, colons, and underscores}
<li>{Duplicate attribute names keep the last value}
}

<p>{When shorthand classes and an HTML class attribute are both present, the values are merged with a space:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p.large-text class="extra">{text}
}}}

<p>{That parses as class equals large-text extra.}

<p>{When shorthand hash-id and an HTML id attribute are both present, the parser throws.}

<h4>{Quoted values inside tags}

<p>{Greater-than characters inside quoted attribute values do not terminate the tag:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p title="1 > 2">{text}
}}}

<h4>{Escape sequences}

<p>{A backslash escapes the next character inside quoted attribute values, flow blocks, and literal blocks.}

<dl>{
<dt>{Backslash followed by an opening curly brace}
<dd>{A literal opening curly brace inside a flow block}
<dt>{Backslash followed by a closing curly brace}
<dd>{A literal closing curly brace inside a flow block}
<dt>{Backslash followed by a double quote}
<dd>{A double quote inside a double-quoted attribute value}
<dt>{Backslash followed by a single quote}
<dd>{A single quote inside a single-quoted attribute value}
<dt>{Backslash followed by a backtick}
<dd>{A backtick inside a backtick-quoted attribute value}
<dt>{Backslash followed by another backslash}
<dd>{A literal backslash}
}

<p>{A backslash before any other character is kept as a literal backslash followed by that character. A trailing backslash immediately before the closing brace or fence is invalid and throws Unexpected end of file.}

<p>{In attribute values:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p title="say \"hello\"">{text}
<input value='it\'s fine'>
}}}

<p>{In flow blocks:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{say "hello"}
<p>{it's fine}
<p>{literal \} brace}
}}}

<p>{In literal blocks, a backslash escapes closing braces and backslashes so they do not end the fence early:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<code>{{{say "hi"\}\}\}}
<code>{{{\}\}\}}
}}}

<p>{The second example parses as a content string of three closing braces.}

<h3>{Blocks}

<p>{After a tag, the parser looks for a block in this order:}

<ol>{
<li>{Literal fence: three opening curly braces}
<li>{Flow block: an opening curly brace}
<li>{Empty block: anything else, including end of file}
}

<h4>{Flow blocks}

<p>{A flow block starts with an opening curly brace and ends with a matching closing brace. Flow blocks hold rich text and inline elements.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{Hello World}
}}}

<p>{An empty flow block opens and immediately closes:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{}
}}}

<p>{Flow blocks preserve whitespace and newlines:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{line one
line two}
}}}

<p>{Use a backslash to include a curly brace in text. See Escape sequences.}

<p>{Inline elements use the same tag-and-brace pattern:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{Hello <strong>{world}}
}}}

<p>{Flow blocks may contain text nodes, element nodes, or both:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{<strong>{bold} <em>{italic}}
}}}

<h4>{Literal blocks}

<p>{Literal blocks use a fence of three opening curly braces and close with three closing curly braces. They are intended for code or other raw text where flow parsing should not run.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<code>{{{
console.log("Hello World")
\}\}\}
}}}

<p>{The opening fence is consumed. Content between the opening and closing fence is stored as a single string. Newlines are preserved. Use a backslash to include braces or a closing fence inside the content. See Escape sequences.}

<p>{An empty literal is valid:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<code>{{\{\}\}\}}
}}}

<p>{Literal fences take precedence over flow blocks. Input starting with an opening triple-brace fence is always treated as a literal opener, not as a flow block followed by extra characters.}

<h4>{Empty blocks}

<p>{An element has an empty block when:}

<ul>{
<li>{It is self-closing}
<li>{The tag is followed immediately by end of file}
<li>{The tag is followed by content that is not a valid block opener}
}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>
<img src="photo.jpg">
}}}

<h3>{Self-closing elements}

<p>{An element is treated as self-closing when the character immediately after the tag, ignoring whitespace, is one of:}

<ul>{
<li>{A less-than sign, which means another element follows}
<li>{The parent flow block closing brace, when that brace is the final character in the source}
}

<p>{No separate slash-greater-than syntax exists.}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<img src="photo.jpg"><p>{Next element}
}}}

<p>{Inside a flow block:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<columns class="border-less" columns="2">{<img src="1.jpg"><img src="2.jpg">}
}}}

<p>{At end of file:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<img src="photo.jpg">
}}}

<p>{If the next character is an opening curly brace and more content follows, the parser treats it as the start of a child flow block:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{<span>{text}}
}}}

<p>{If the next character is plain text or whitespace, the element gets an empty block:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{before <img src="photo.jpg"> after}
}}}

<h3>{Nesting}

<p>{Nesting happens in two ways:}

<ol>{
<li>{Flow nesting: child elements appear inside a parent flow block}
<li>{Sibling elements: consecutive tags at the same level}
}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<div>{<p>{<strong>{deep\}\}\}}
}}}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<h1>{Title}<p>{Body}
}}}

<p>{Without a flow block, consecutive tags are siblings, not parent and child:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p><strong>{bold}
}}}

<p>{That parses as an empty p element followed by a strong element containing bold text.}

<h2>{AST}

<p>{parse returns a document node:}

<code lang="typescript">{{{
{
  type: "document",
  children: ElementNode[]
}
}}}

<h3>{Node types}

<dl>{
<dt>{document}
<dd>{Root node containing top-level elements}
<dt>{element}
<dd>{A tag name, attributes, and a block}
<dt>{flow}
<dd>{Rich text and inline child nodes}
<dt>{text}
<dd>{Plain text inside a flow block}
<dt>{literal}
<dd>{Raw fenced string content}
<dt>{empty}
<dd>{No block content}
}

<h3>{Element node}

<code lang="typescript">{{{
{
  type: "element",
  tag: {
    tag: string,
    attributes: Record<string, string>
  },
  block: FlowBlockNode | LiteralBlockNode | EmptyNodeBlock
}
}}}

<p>{Boolean attributes are stored as empty strings.}

<h3>{Flow block node}

<code lang="typescript">{{{
{
  type: "flow",
  children: (ElementNode | TextNode)[]
}
}}}

<p>{If a flow block opens and closes with no content, the block is empty rather than flow.}

<h3>{Literal block node}

<code lang="typescript">{{{
{
  type: "literal",
  content: string
}
}}}

<h2>{Errors}

<p>{The parser throws a ParseError for invalid input. ParseError extends the built-in Error and formats its message in the style of compiler diagnostics: the line and column of the offending span, a snippet of the offending line, a caret pointing at the span, and an optional help hint.}

<code lang="ts">{{{
import { parse, ParseError } from "cntx";

try {
  parse('<p>{unclosed');
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ParseError) {
    console.error(error.message);
    console.error("line:", error.line, "column:", error.column);
  }
}
}}}

<p>{The message above prints as:}

<code lang="text">{{{
error: Unexpected end of file
  --> 1:4
  |
1 | <p>{unclosed
  |    ^ unclosed flow block
  |
  = help: flow block is missing its closing `}`
}}}

<h3>{ParseError fields}

<dl>{
<dt>{code}
<dd>{The error code (one of the ErrorMessages enum values)}
<dt>{source}
<dd>{The original source string that was parsed}
<dt>{index}
<dd>{Zero-based character offset of the start of the offending span}
<dt>{length}
<dd>{Length of the offending span, in characters}
<dt>{line}
<dd>{One-based line number of the span start}
<dt>{column}
<dd>{One-based column number of the span start}
<dt>{label}
<dd>{Short label shown next to the caret (may be undefined)}
<dt>{hint}
<dd>{Optional help hint shown below the snippet (may be undefined)}
}

<p>{The ErrorMessages enum and an isParseError type guard are also exported.}

<h3>{Error codes}

<dl>{
<dt>{Unexpected end of file}
<dd>{Unclosed flow block, unclosed literal fence, unclosed quoted attribute value, or a trailing backslash before a closing brace or fence}
<dt>{Unexpected character}
<dd>{Input does not start with a tag, or extra content appears after a complete element}
<dt>{Missing Tag Close}
<dd>{Tag is missing a closing greater-than sign, or an attribute quote is not closed before the tag ends}
<dt>{Missing tag}
<dd>{Empty tag name}
<dt>{Empty ID}
<dd>{Shorthand id with no value}
<dt>{Empty Class}
<dd>{Shorthand class with no value}
<dt>{Multiple IDs}
<dd>{Both shorthand and HTML id attributes on the same tag}
<dt>{Equals cannot be an attribute}
<dd>{Malformed attribute starting with an equals sign}
<dt>{Quote must follow equals}
<dd>{Attribute value is missing opening quotes}
}

<p>{Invalid examples:}

<code lang="cntx">{{{
<p>{unclosed
<code>{{{unclosed
<p title="unclosed
<p>{hello\\
<p#foo id="bar">{text}
{hello}
hello<p>{world}
}}}

<h2>{Limitations}

<ul>{
<li>{Attribute values must be quoted. HTML-style unquoted values are not supported. This is intentional.}
<li>{The package exports parse only. Rendering, formatting, and validation beyond parsing are out of scope.}
}

<h2>{Development}

<code lang="bash">{{{
pnpm install
pnpm test
pnpm typecheck
pnpm build
}}}

